{
  "name": "1940_sidi_barrani",
  "title": "Operation Compass: Sidi Barrani, Dec 1940",
  "notes": "Operation Compass, 9-11 Dec 1940. Western Desert Force (O'Connor) vs the Italian 10th Army's fortified camps. Researched (Playfair Vol.I, Wikipedia Operation Compass OOB per Montanari 1990/Christie 1999, Maletti Group/1st-2nd Libyan Div/63rd Cirene/64th Catanzaro/4th CC.NN. articles). AXES: the WDF marched from Mersa Matruh (E) via Bir Kenayis, passed through the Nibeiwa-Rabia gap and struck the camps from the desert flank (SW); dirs=E (coast road, Selby-style approach) + SW (main desert-flank attack) mirror that. ATTACKER (25 bns): 4th Indian Division (Beresford-Peirse) — 5th Ind Bde (1/R.Fus, 3/1.Punjab, 4/6.RajRif), 11th Ind Bde (1/6.RajRif, 2.Camerons, 4/7.Rajput), 16th Br Bde (2.Queen's, 1.A&SH, 2.Leicester), 7.RTR (47 Matilda IIs, led every wire break-in), div art (1st+25th Field + 7th Medium Regts RA); 7th Armoured Division (Caunter) — 4th Armd Bde (7.Hussars Mk VI, 2.RTR+6.RTR cruisers), 7th Armd Bde (3.KOH Mk VI, 8.KRIH Mk VI, 1.RTR cruisers), Support Group (1.KRRC+2.Rifle Bde motor battalions), 11.Hussars armoured cars, 3.RHA, 106th Lancs Yeomanry (AT), 2nd HAA Rgt. DEFENDER (29 bns): Raggruppamento Maletti at Nibeiwa (I/V/XVII/XIX Libyan bns + I Saharan bn, motorized; II Carri M bn M11/39; 65/17+75/27 groups); 2nd Libyan Division at Tummar West/East + Pt90 (II/VI/VII + XIV/XV/XVI Libyan bns, IX Carri L L3/35, 2 Libyan art groups, II Genio); 4th CC.NN. '3 Gennaio' in the town (228th+250th Legions, 204th Art Rgt); 1st Libyan Division remnants trapped in the town pocket (VIII/X/XII, org 35). EXCLUDED (out of the battle province and historically escaping): 63rd Cirene (Rabia/Sofafi — never attacked, withdrew to Halfaya), 64th Catanzaro (Alam Salamus/Buq Buq), 132nd Ariete (stayed in Italy — Playfair explicit; only 4th Tank Rgt's II Bn M was in Egypt), XXI Corps L3 battalions (Buq Buq). Terrain: pure desert (def -15%, no cover) + coast; VP1 town = the city flag. Italian colonial/blackshirt under-strength (org 45/30/35); Maletti motorized (the only mobile force — truck-borne). Stats = 1939 calibration: Matilda heavy_armor 70 (immune to 47/32 AT piercing 45); 2-pdr cruisers pierce 55 (M11 armor 30 is vulnerable); L3/Mk VI machine-gun tanks piercing 5.",
